AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(obo:IAO_0000115 "The double compound muscle action potential (CMAP) or double “M wave” is a recording from a muscle as a result of motor nerve stimulation. It is a duplication of the fundamental signal in motor nerve conduction and related studies (e.g., F waves, H reflex, repetitive motor nerve stimulation, etc.). It is a double banal, simple waveform observable through instrumentation. "@en) Annotation(rdfs:label "Doble anomalía del potencial de acción motora compuesta"@es) Annotation(rdfs:label "Double anomalie du CMAP"@fr) Annotation(rdfs:label "Double compound motor action potential abnormality"@en) rdfs:label obo:PROMOT_0000106 "Double compound motor action potential abnormality"@en)
